#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435679} :activity/id #uuid "26e5acff-8db9-5e5d-9122-36baf139baac" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049340 :topic/id #uuid "ecf075bf-6d18-5a77-93a9-57ef73f45115" :topic/math-academy-id 1869} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "293235d4-a2f2-5777-a667-1540f003765f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435670} {:answer/id #uuid "46090913-fe8a-53d8-a2e2-1edec9407dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435671} {:answer/id #uuid "596e4b3c-1fd0-573a-82a9-d1617135d478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435672} {:answer/id #uuid "75acd049-7010-5a98-8813-f29e53e8c979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435673} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2003c1-be5a-5ec0-8d3f-914e8ee86a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435674} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9f16a7-f4b2-5dc6-b4b7-1d7e51e453fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6" :question/math-academy-id "q-79349" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nIII. $A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=5$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "42d8e8b3-7048-5f94-884b-ae373fb59042" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188d8c1d-5896-5f10-81c9-bd96ad0517aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269475} {:answer/id #uuid "52e6f0c7-0a62-59e3-a5cb-80e9b7f54638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270005} {:answer/id #uuid "54208619-14dc-516d-b1aa-20ed09a0bb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270018} {:answer/id #uuid "77353fd7-ee88-5664-aec8-e00589b061d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270324} {:answer/id #uuid "af2612fc-39ba-5012-92ba-66032676ab46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270827}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186270827} :answer-field/id #uuid "94b73dce-7f8c-597e-ae8e-4e20e2b2ff1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8dad0d98-37c5-5af9-9c0a-4f0fabec2bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141200" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "9a467517-2fb7-54c3-b455-e47e7392ef56"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435679 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef04a305-48e9-5100-9ee7-37ef95dd031d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121779} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ebd6d4-ef22-55d1-b2fd-1d2f280fa42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121780} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1a9ac3-b9a3-59ca-891f-c8d93f27fd0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121781} {:answer/id #uuid "62f0ec41-6c5f-51cb-9439-22250619fa40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121782} {:answer/id #uuid "730f0ca8-ac97-51bf-ae0d-7facf7eedff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121782} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d952797-9510-50c2-afac-7e03150f3737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a5b63a26-4713-5ecd-9d64-befaccc0bd77" :question/math-academy-id "q-34834" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "d2193342-5bc1-5a6f-99d1-42bf1fad6047" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435677}}] :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435669}]}
